Today is Friday evening.
My doorbell rings.
I open the door.
Outside, my friend Asha is standing.
With her is her dog, Moti.
In Asha's hand is a heavy bag of dog food.
In her other hand is Moti's leash.
Asha says, "Maya, thank you very, very much."
"You are looking after Moti this weekend."
"I am going out of town tomorrow morning."
I smile and call her inside.
I say, "No problem, Asha."
"I like Moti very much."
Asha gives me that heavy bag.
She tells me, "Keep this bag inside."
"And take this leash of his."
I take the bag and the leash.
Moti happily wags his tail.
I bend down and pet him lovingly.
Asha says to Moti, "Moti, sit quietly here now."
I tell Asha, "Don't you worry at all."
"We both will have a lot of fun."
